OAB - Anaesthesiologists are generally well prepared for managing 
      LAST.Anaesthesiologists with less than 10 years of experience demonstrated 
      greater preparedness compared to their colleagues with more than 20 years of 
      experience.Atypical symptoms of LAST are commonly overlooked by 
      anaesthesiologists as presentation of LAST.Areas needing enhancement include the 
      awareness of anaesthesiologists regarding the precise location of the lipid 
      emulsion in case of an emergency, the availability of lipid emulsion and 
      cognitive aids, as well as the retrieval process for lipid emulsion.
