OAB - Postoperative sleep disturbance occurs in 22.8–44.0% of patients. Surgery 
      disrupts sleep cycles and alters brain wave patterns through elevated stress 
      hormone levels and other mechanisms.Multiple perioperative factors influence 
      postoperative sleep quality. These include patient age, preexisting conditions 
      such as coronary artery disease, postoperative pain and environmental 
      conditions.Research on sleep quality during the early postoperative period after 
      caesarean delivery is limited. The associated factors and effects on early 
      breastfeeding remain poorly understood.
